{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795827927,"nonce":"1FTmh493pSXTq8ODNy+WEbmfj5g=","message":"Fixed in f582f8d0b5bbba99c5f03a9cf72812c204659ea8.\n\nThe layout editor takes a top inset (set_code_top_inset). Rows, gutter, caret, selection, matches, diagnostics, minimap, hit testing and scroll-into-view use it. The cn bar and the editor's built-in bar both set it to their height while open and to zero when closed. A view that is scrolled keeps its text in place unless that would leave the cursor covered.\n\nFound on the way: the editor reads the search query back from the built-in bar's field when it draws, so a query set before the bar opened was cleared by the first redraw. The bar's field now starts from the query.","files":null}]}